This Python function uses iterative deepening depth-first search to find a path between two cells in a grid. The function works by maintaining a frontier (queue) of cells to visit. It starts with the goal as the only cell in the frontier, and repeatedly tries to move to a neighboring cell.  As the search is made deeper, a maximal number of farther away nodes of the frontier (called polynomial pruning) are removed so as to maintain a constant time complexity for staying in the frontier.  The process continues until a path from the start to the goal is found.

